meta {
  name: Write today's entry with a photo
  type: http
  seq: 32
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/entries
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "text": "Look at the light on the wall this morning.",
    "imageMediaId": "{{mediaId}}"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  // A new key on every send, as Write today's entry makes one.
  req.setHeader("Idempotency-Key", require("uuid").v4());
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setVar("entryId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  An entry with a photo (ADR-0048): the photo Media upload intent named, once Media says it is READY. Its owner only, READY, and on no other entry: anything else is 422 VALIDATION_FAILED on imageMediaId, one answer whatever the reason, and no entry is written. The 201 carries `image` with its status READY, a signed URL and its size; the partner, once the day reveals, sees the same photo as PROCESSING, with no URL, until it has passed moderation (D4). A locked entry says nothing of a photo.

  Bruno's Media upload sends twenty bytes of text, which the pipeline refuses (FAILED): to try this request, upload a real JPEG, PNG, HEIC or WebP (`scripts/smoke.sh`'s photos section shows how with curl), then set mediaId to its id. A voice note goes the same way (Write today's entry with a voice note).
}
